Certainly! Below are the three core files required to create a custom Node-RED node named `Pankaj`:

---

**1. `package.json`**

This file defines your node’s metadata and dependencies.

```json
{
  "name": "node-red-contrib-pankaj",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "A simple Node-RED node named Pankaj",
  "dependencies": {},
  "keywords": [
    "node-red",
    "node-red-node"
  ],
  "node-red": {
    "nodes": {
      "pankaj": "pankaj.js"
    }
  },
  "author": "Your Name",
  "license": "MIT"
}
```

---

**2. `pankaj.html`**

This file defines the node’s appearance and configuration in the Node-RED editor.

```html
<script type="text/javascript">
    RED.nodes.registerType('pankaj',{
        category: 'function',
        color: "#a6bbcf",
        defaults: {
            name: {value:""}
        },
        inputs:1,
        outputs:1,
        icon: "font-awesome/fa-user",
        label: function() {
            return this.name||"Pankaj";
        }
    });
</script>

<script type="text/x-red" data-template-name="pankaj">
    <div class="form-row">
        <label for="node-input-name"><i class="fa fa-tag"></i> Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="node-input-name" placeholder="Name">
    </div>
</script>

<script type="text/x-red" data-help-name="pankaj">
    <p>
        The <b>Pankaj</b> node is a sample custom node for Node-RED.
    </p>
    <p>
        It passes the input message through and can be expanded for custom logic.
    </p>
</script>
```

---

**3. `pankaj.js`**

This is the server-side JavaScript file defining the node’s runtime behavior.

```javascript
module.exports = function(RED) {
    function PankajNode(config) {
        RED.nodes.createNode(this, config);
        var node = this;
        node.on('input', function(msg, send, done) {
            // Add any custom logic here
            msg.pankaj = "Hello from Pankaj!";
            send(msg);
            if (done) {
                done();
            }
        });
    }
    RED.nodes.registerType("pankaj", PankajNode);
}
```

---

**Usage Notes:**
- Place all three files in the same directory.
- Install the node to Node-RED (using `npm install PATH_TO_YOUR_FOLDER`) or link it during development.
- The node will simply add a property `msg.pankaj` with a greeting, and can be expanded for further functionality.

